<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Belovezha Accords</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1991</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Białowieża Accords</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Belovezha Accords were signed on 8 December 1991 at Viskuli in the Belovezha Forest of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/belarus">Belarus</a> by the leaders of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ukraine">Ukraine</a> and Belarus: <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boris-yeltsin">Boris Yeltsin</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leonid-kravchuk">Leonid Kravchuk</a> and Stanislav Shushkevich. They declared that the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/soviet-union">Soviet Union</a> had ceased to exist and founded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/commonwealth-of-independent-states">Commonwealth of Independent States</a>. The Soviet Union was formally dissolved on 26 December 1991.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/belovezha-accords.jpg" alt="Belovezha Accords" width="320" height="210" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: U. Ivanov / Ю. Иванов · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RIAN_archive_848095_Signing_the_Agreement_to_eliminate_the_USSR_and_establish_the_Commonwealth_of_Independent_States.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
